/bin/
*.wasm
/rust/target/

# Exception: the modules that published benchmark numbers were produced with.
# bin/ is a build output and *.wasm is ignored, so until this negation existed
# the module a published figure was measured with lived in exactly one place -
# an untracked working copy, one `make build-wasm` away from being gone. The
# md5 is in each filename and is what run fingerprints record, so these are
# provenance, not build artifacts. Never regenerate one in place; add a new
# file under its own md5 instead.
!/rust/testdata/published-modules/
!/rust/testdata/published-modules/*.wasm
